/applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJI PHOTO FILM CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INOUE, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATANABE, HIDETOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>AMIMORI ICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>INOUE HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WATANABE HIDETOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AMIMORI, ICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INOUE, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATANABE, HIDETOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A matlike high-transmittance film comprises a transparent support (1), a hardcoat layer (2) containing particles (4) whose size ranges 1.0-10  mu m and is larger than the thickness of the transparent support (1), and a low refractive index layer (3) covering the hardcoat layer and having a refractive index of 1.45 or less. The haze of the film is 1.0 % or more and the total light transmittance is 93.5 % or more. The high-transmittance film can prevent uneven display due to thermal expansion of a light control film and uneven brightness peculiar to the light control film.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un film à haute transmittance de type tapis, qui comprend un support transparent (1), une couche de protection dure (2) contenant des particules (4) dont la taille est comprise entre 1,0 et 10  mu m et supérieure à l'épaisseur du support transparent (1), et une couche à faible indice de réfraction (3) recouvrant la couche de protection dure et présentant un indice de réfraction d'au plus 1,45. Le trouble du film est d'au moins 1,0 % et la transmission totale de la lumière est d'au moins 93,5 %. Ce film à haute transmittance peut empêcher un affichage inégal dû à une dilatation thermique d'un film anti-reflet et une luminosité inégale spécifique au film anti-reflet.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>